          "lines": [
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Steps"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "1. Read the request in your prompt: its inputs, every acceptance criterion and the deliverable. The criteria come from the contract and can only be met, never changed; copy the relevant ones verbatim into every task you delegate."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "2. Delegate to `writer` (Writer) with `budget=3`: its part of the request, with the criteria it must meet."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "3. When the work exists, delegate to `reviewer` (Independent Reviewer) with `budget=2` to check the final file independently against every criterion. It reports findings and required changes to you and never edits the author's file."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "4. If a check fails: send the required changes, quoted verbatim, to the AUTHOR of the failing file (`delegate(to=<author>, revises=<that author's task id>, budget=1)`; for the deliverable usually `writer`), then have the checker re-check that same file (`delegate(to=<checker>, revises=<the checker's task id>)`). One rework and one re-check; if it still fails, report `blocked` with options and the checker's final line instead of starting another cycle."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "5. Read the final artifact yourself and check it against EVERY criterion of the request, quoting counts from your own `read` output, and paste the checker's final coverage line verbatim."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "6. Report: `done` only if every criterion is met (else `blocked` with the deviation and a recommended decision). Name the deliverable's path (the assistant copies it to /tmp/hirearchy-g0-m0-s2-1792995184/deliverables) and pass `lessons`: 1-3 lines for the next request - what worked, what to change in this playbook, and the evidence (runs used, rework, review findings)."
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "## Budget plan"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "Request budget: 12 runs (the contract's). Hand down no more than this up front, each with `budget=` set explicitly:"
            },
            {
              "own_words": false,
              "text": "- writer: 3 runs (2 work + 1 rework or re-check)"
            }
          ],
